# rb.sh's build server per worktree (11-01): the first line whose pattern matches the worktree's directory name
# (a bash glob) wins; no match: vibe4. Each worktree keeps its warm target dir on its own host.
# 11-06 (lead): spread so no host sits idle. vibe4 (16 cores, 62 GB): the land checks plus bool (replay corpora).
# vibe5 (16 cores, 29 GB): psui, skasm, core (11-07 17:55: vibe2 at 23 with core + qa, vibe5 at 2). vibe4 also dx.
# vibe2 (8 cores, 31 GB): qa's model suite and heavy one-off probes.
# vibe3 (8 cores, 31 GB): asm and qa. This machine runs Chrome for live/live2: build on your host through rb.sh, not here.
# Heavy one-off probes: NOSHAPE_RB_HOST=<the idlest host>.
bool*     vibe4
core*     vibe5
blend*    vibe5
dev*      vibe4
psui*     vibe5
skasm*    vibe5
dx*       vibe4
asm*      vibe3
studios*  vibe3
cliapp*   vibe5
appicon*  vibe5
bool2*    vibe4
*         vibe4
